h3-go — a pure-Go implementation of Uber's H3 geospatial indexing system.

This project is a derivative work of Uber's H3 library
(https://github.com/uber/h3):

- H3: Copyright (c) 2016-2025 Uber Technologies, Inc.
- H3 is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see the LICENSE
  file in the H3 repository for details.

The Go implementation is a function-by-function translation of the H3 C
sources (currently targeting the version reported by the package's
Version* constants). Each ported declaration carries a
"Ported from H3 C: <file>::<name>" attribution comment, and
docs/c-api-inventory.csv maps the complete C API surface to its Go
counterparts.

No H3 C source files are vendored in this repository. The opt-in parity
test suite (build tags `cgo && c2go`) downloads pristine upstream H3
sources into `testref/` at test time and compiles them for in-process
comparison against the Go implementation; that infrastructure is excluded
from every normal build of this module, which is pure Go with no cgo and
no dependencies.

